Pick one model for server-side one-shot AI calls, native first

The model-picking rule that the AI rewrite button used (try a native API key provider first because it answers in under a second, leave Ollama out of that pass because it always claims to be configured, then fall back to whatever models were discovered) now lives in one exported function, pickOneShotModel, in the chat providers service, so the upcoming Start work planner can use the same rule instead of a copy. It walks anthropic then openai then gemini first, then honours PAPERCLIP_CHAT_DEFAULT_MODEL when no native provider is set up and that model's own provider is, then ranks the discovered adapter and Ollama models exactly as pickBestDefaultModel does, and returns null when nothing at all is configured rather than the hardcoded claude-opus-4-7. The environment variable sits below the native pass on purpose: it is the chat session default and is routinely pointed at an adapter model, so honouring it first would make every one-shot call cold-start a CLI. The ranking was split into a small private helper shared by both functions so a one-shot call does not run adapter discovery and the Ollama probe twice. The AI rewrite route now calls pickOneShotModel and answers 503 with a plain 'No AI model is configured' message when it returns null. Tests cover the native preference (with a fetch spy proving Ollama is never probed), the native order, the adapter fallthrough agreeing with pickBestDefaultModel, the null case, the environment variable being honoured only when no native provider is set up, the native default beating a servable environment choice, an explicit choice whose provider has no key falling through to discovery, and the route's two branches.

